WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.380
You're ready to finish.

2
00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:03.100
The website isn't.

3
00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.500
A bus-pass application.

4
00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:07.220
A tool you need to use your phone.

5
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.400
A checkout button that stays just out of reach.

6
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:14.020
One broken step can turn an ordinary task into

7
00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:16.100
asking somebody else for help.

8
00:00:16.293 --> 00:00:18.573
We built Can I Finish to change that.

9
00:00:18.982 --> 00:00:21.462
Start with the thing a person came to do.

10
00:00:21.689 --> 00:00:22.749
Set a clear destination.

11
00:00:23.809 --> 00:00:27.649
Our browser runner follows the keyboard journey, captures what

12
00:00:27.669 --> 00:00:30.549
happens, and gives your team evidence they can act

13
00:00:30.569 --> 00:00:33.602
on. Every run connects a human goal to an

14
00:00:33.622 --> 00:00:34.782
observable result.

15
00:00:35.182 --> 00:00:36.662
Take a real public service.

16
00:00:37.042 --> 00:00:39.862
Find where to apply for a disabled person's bus

17
00:00:39.882 --> 00:00:42.302
pass on GOV dot UK.

18
00:00:42.922 --> 00:00:45.962
The browser follows the keyboard route, opens the application

19
00:00:45.982 --> 00:00:48.082
page, and checks the destination.

20
00:00:48.102 --> 00:00:50.142
Twenty-six key events.

21
00:00:50.162 --> 00:00:52.102
Twenty-eight evidence frames.

22
00:00:52.682 --> 00:00:55.202
That's a concrete answer to a question that matters:

23
00:00:55.222 --> 00:00:57.362
can someone get where they need to go?

24
00:00:57.885 --> 00:01:01.345
Now Apple. Find the iPhone VoiceOver setup guide, using

25
00:01:01.365 --> 00:01:04.585
the keyboard. The journey reaches the actual support article.

26
00:01:04.985 --> 00:01:06.745
Different website. Different goal.

27
00:01:07.205 --> 00:01:10.245
The same evidence-driven workflow, focused on what a person

28
00:01:10.265 --> 00:01:11.225
came to do.

29
00:01:11.618 --> 00:01:14.758
And when the journey breaks, the evidence gets specific.

30
00:01:15.558 --> 00:01:18.998
In our Field Notes checkout, eighteen Tab presses never

31
00:01:19.018 --> 00:01:20.458
reach the payment control.

32
00:01:20.798 --> 00:01:22.498
The focus trail shows the barrier.

33
00:01:23.058 --> 00:01:25.838
The AI proposal points toward a native button.

34
00:01:26.038 --> 00:01:29.078
Change the control, run the same task again, and

35
00:01:29.098 --> 00:01:32.278
the PayPal handoff succeeds in four key events.

36
00:01:32.684 --> 00:01:35.664
Keep the screenshot, the exact steps, and an executable

37
00:01:35.684 --> 00:01:38.864
regression test. The next release gets the same finish

38
00:01:38.884 --> 00:01:41.884
line. Developers get something they can reproduce.

39
00:01:42.784 --> 00:01:44.624
Teams get a repair they can verify.

40
00:01:45.524 --> 00:01:48.204
And accessibility becomes part of how the product ships.

41
00:01:48.651 --> 00:01:51.511
Because on the other side of every interface is

42
00:01:51.531 --> 00:01:53.391
someone trying to move forward.

43
00:01:53.891 --> 00:01:54.751
Can I Finish.

44
00:01:55.271 --> 00:01:56.191
Find the barrier.

45
00:01:56.751 --> 00:01:57.491
Prove the repair.

46
00:01:57.991 --> 00:01:59.691
Build a web people can finish.